id: pm-glmcnd
title: Release publication downloads the producer-binding artifact once and blocks the daily cut when the download endpoint trails the listing
description: "The blocker_retry Auto Release run 45818705282 on 2026-11-26 passed every gate, uploaded release-producer-binding-1 (artifact 15118638954, finalized 12:56:28.2Z), found it in a complete inventory on the first read, and failed 1.5 s later in recordReleasePublicationOrigin: gh run download returned HTTP 404 for actions/artifacts/15118638954/zip. Nothing was pushed or published and blocker issue GH-1788 was reopened with a retry marker, so only a manual dispatch could still cut the day's release. pm-jvb9pk made the inventory read wait out a trailing listing; the download of a listed artifact is a second read of the same eventually consistent store and still runs once, so a not-yet-servable archive costs the whole daily release exactly as a trailing listing did."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[4]: "area:release",auto-release,"gh:1788",reliability
created_at: "2026-11-26T14:22:25.576Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-26T17:43:27.300Z"
closed_at: "2026-11-26T17:43:27.277Z"
completed_at: "2026-11-26T17:43:27.277Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: "The publication gate downloads the selected binding again after a bounded wait when the provider answers HTTP 404, each attempt into a fresh directory; Any other download failure, and a 404 that outlasts the wait, is refused at once with the provider's error; the downloaded file is verified exactly as before; A spec drives trailing 404 downloads, a persistent 404 and a non-404 failure through the gate and proves the waits and refusals; GH-1788 carries a root-cause comment naming this item"
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "downloadProducerBinding retries only an HTTP 404 download after the bounded waits of the inventory read (1, 2, 4, 8, 15 s), each attempt into a fresh directory; after the download the inventory is read again with the same waits and must still hold exactly the validated artifact id, so a visible replacement is refused at once"
expected_result: "A producer binding listed in the complete inventory is downloaded and verified, and the release is pushed"
actual_result: "release-tag-provenance.spec.ts proves trailing, persistent and non-404 download failures, a replaced binding and a partial post-download listing; GH-1788 carries the root-cause comment"
dependencies[1]{id,kind,created_at,author,source_kind,author_source}:
  pm-jvb9pk,discovered_from,"2026-11-26T14:22:25.576Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T16:52:11.580Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 2 on PR #1789: gh run download addresses the binding by name, so a retried download could fetch a replacement artifact uploaded under the same name. After the download, the gate now reads the inventory once more and requires exactly the artifact it validated (same id; an id is now part of a declared binding). The spec drives a replacement during a 404 retry to the new refusal and refuses bindings without a positive id."
  "2026-11-26T17:06:00.496Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 3 on PR #1789: (1) fixed: the inventory read after the download now uses the same bounded rereads as the first read, so a partial listing is waited out instead of refused, while a replaced, duplicate or invalid binding is still refused at once. (2) Declined, download by artifact id: the downloaded file is verified against the actual tag object (schema, tag, tag and object SHAs, and the full provenance record), so any archive that passes carries exactly the attested binding; gh run download <run-id> resolves only artifacts of the producer run; the post-download read refuses a replacement or duplicate; the reviewer's stub, where a name resolves to an id the listing does not show, is not a state the provider presents. Pinning the id would mean extracting the zip in-process on the release path for no verification gain."
  "2026-11-26T17:16:21.763Z","harness:claude-code","Codex review round 4 on PR #1789: a post-download listing that shows a binding other than the validated id, even while partial, is now refused without waiting; a partial listing of the validated binding is still read again within the bounded wait."
files[2]{path,scope,note}:
